  "worked_solution": "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=\u27e83+2t,4t,-4+3t\u27e9.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y+4z-60 & =0 \\\\ 4x+3y+4z & =60 \\\\ \u27e8x,y,z\u27e9\\cdot \u27e84,3,4\u27e9 & =60 \\\\ r\\cdot \u27e84,3,4\u27e9 & =60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=\u27e83+2t,4t,-4+3t\u27e9$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot \u27e84,3,4\u27e9 & =60 \\\\ \u27e83+2t,4t,-4+3t\u27e9\\cdot \u27e84,3,4\u27e9 & =60 \\\\ 4(3+2t)+3(4t)+4(-4+3t) & =60 \\\\ 12+8t+12t-16+12t & =60 \\\\ 32t & =64 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =\u27e83+2(2),4(2),-4+3(2)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e87,8,2\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(7,8,2).$",
